```html
<h1>Arm Robot Simulation</h1>
<p>
This project demonstrates a robotic arm simulation built in Webots, where the arm is tasked with detecting, picking up, and placing bottles into crates.
</p>

<p>
The project applies <b>Forward Kinematics (FK)</b> and <b>Inverse Kinematics (IK)</b> concepts:
<ul>
  <li><b>Forward Kinematics (FK):</b> Calculating the position and orientation of the robot’s end-effector from given joint parameters.</li>
  <li><b>Inverse Kinematics (IK):</b> Determining the required joint angles to reach a specific target position for object manipulation.</li>
</ul>
</p>

<h3>Demo Screenshot</h3>
<p>Below is an example of the arm robot environment in Webots:</p>

<img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ddf58f43-5572-4017-8b8c-7a208b334aea" alt="Screenshot 2024-07-13 222813" width="600"/>

<h3>How to Run</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Install Webots: <a href="https://cyberbotics.com/#download">Download here</a></li>
  <li>Clone this repository:
    <pre><code>
    git clone https://github.com/farah50/Webots_tasks.git
    cd Webots_tasks/Arm\ Robot
    </code></pre>
  </li>
  <li>Open <code>ArmRobot.wbt</code> in Webots.</li>
  <li>Run the simulation to see the robotic arm perform pick-and-place tasks.</li>
</ol>
